 Here's every logo and favicon file in the repo, plus the code that points to them. Most are still Twenty's artwork, and several load straight from Twenty's own servers.

  1. Main CRM app (packages/twenty-front), which matters most for the rebrand

  Image files
  - public/images/icons/android/android-launchericon-{48,72,96,144,192,512}.png
  - public/images/icons/ios/*.png: 26 sizes, from 16 to 1024
  - public/images/icons/windows11/*: tiles, splash screens, store logo and app icons in many sizes
  - public/images/integrations/twenty-logo.svg
  - public/images/onboarding/welcome-halftone.svg: onboarding artwork that may include the brand
  - public/manifest.json: lists the icons above. The name there is already "Cybernetics".

  Code that points to them
  - index.html:6-13: the browser tab icon (android-launchericon-48-48.png), the iPhone home-screen icon (ios/192.png) and the manifest link.
  - index.html:17-26: the link-preview image still points at Twenty's GitHub social-card.png.
  - src/modules/ui/utilities/page-favicon/components/PageFavicon.tsx: sets the browser tab icon while the app runs. It falls back to DEFAULT_WORKSPACE_LOGO.
  - src/modules/ui/navigation/navigation-drawer/constants/DefaultWorkspaceLogo.ts: loads a Twenty logo from Twenty's own site (twentyhq.github.io/.../twenty-logo.png). These files use it:
    - PageFavicon.tsx
    - SignInUpGlobalScopeForm.tsx
    - three files under MultiWorkspaceDropdown/
    - SettingsAdminWorkspaceContent.tsx
    - SettingsAdminUserDetail.tsx
    - SettingsAdminWorkspaceDetail.tsx
  - src/modules/auth/components/Logo.tsx:62: the logo on the login (/welcome) page, which uses android-launchericon-192-192.png.
  - twenty-logo.svg is used in:
    - applications/components/AppConnectionHeader.tsx:69
    - onboarding/components/OnboardingHeader.tsx:61
    - onboarding/components/OnboardingPulsingLogo.tsx:26
    - onboarding/components/import-contacts/OnboardingImportPreviewSyncBadge.tsx:49

  2. Emails (packages/twenty-emails)

  - src/components/Logo.tsx:10: hardcoded to https://app.twenty.com/images/icons/windows11/Square150x150Logo.scale-100.png.
  - src/constants/DefaultWorkspaceLogo.ts: loads the Twenty logo from Twenty's site. It's used in validate-approved-access-domain.email.tsx.

  3. Server

  - twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/dev-seeder/core/constants/seeder-workspaces.constant.ts: the demo workspaces' logos load from Twenty's site.

  4. Marketing website (packages/twenty-website)

  - src/app/favicon.ico
  - public/images/core/logo.svg
  - public/images/shared/companies/logos/twenty.svg
  - public/images/shared/halftone/twenty-logo.svg
  - Logos drawn directly in code: src/icons/TwentyLogo.tsx and src/app-preview/primitives/FaviconLogo.tsx

  5. Docs site (packages/twenty-docs)

  - favicon.png and logo.svg, both set in docs.json:6-9
  - images/core/logo.svg and images/core/logo-mini.png

  6. Other packages with Twenty branding

  - twenty-ui/logo.png
  - twenty-companion (desktop app):
    - twenty.icns: the macOS app icon
    - src/assets/twenty-logo.svg
    - src/assets/twenty-logo-256.png, used in src/main.js:12
    - src/assets/avatar.svg
  - twenty-codex-plugin/assets/twenty-logo.{png,svg}, set in .codex-plugin/plugin.json:46-47
  - twenty-sdk/src/cli/utilities/build/cover/assets/twenty-logo-mark-path.ts: the logo is drawn in code for app cover images.
  - create-twenty-app: src/constants/template/public/logo.svg, and its README shows the logo from Twenty's GitHub.
  - twenty-docker/helm/twenty/Chart.yaml:7: the Helm chart icon loads from Twenty's GitHub.

  Not your brand (you can skip these)

  - Third-party logos:
    - everything in twenty-front/public/images/integrations/ except twenty-logo.svg
    - twenty-website/public/images/logo-bar/*
    - everything in twenty-website/public/images/shared/companies/logos/ except twenty.svg
  - Logos and favicons of the sample and marketplace apps in twenty-apps/*
  - The IconBrand* icons in twenty-ui, which are for AI providers
  - Code for uploading a workspace logo, and getLinkFaviconUrl / getLogoUrlFromDomainName, which fetch other companies' favicons

  For the app itself, the quickest changes are:
  - the icon files under twenty-front/public/images/icons/
  - twenty-logo.svg
  - the two DefaultWorkspaceLogo.ts files
  - twenty-emails/src/components/Logo.tsx
  - the link-preview image lines in index.html
